WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:07.041
Dick and Mr. Hobbs weren't the only ones surprised by the arrival of a new Lord Fauntleroy.

2
00:00:07.042 --> 00:00:13.027
Everyone who lived in or around Dorincourt Castle was talking about it.

3
00:00:13.028 --> 00:00:18.739
The earl, Mr. Havisham, and the servants all had opinions about the situation.

4
00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:24.331
Everyone hoped that Cedric would prove to be the real heir.

5
00:00:24.332 --> 00:00:29.861
Out in the stables, Wilkins groomed Cedric's pony with extra care.

6
00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:38.806
"It'll be a sad day if that young man no longer comes to the stables," he said to the pony.

7
00:00:38.807 --> 00:00:45.181
Of course Cedric had some questions, but he waited awhile to ask the earl.

8
00:00:45.182 --> 00:00:50.911
One afternoon, as they sat in the library, Cedric decided to speak up.

9
00:00:50.912 --> 00:00:58.641
"This new Lord Fauntleroy and his mother—will they take Mama's house and carriage?"

10
00:00:58.642 --> 00:01:04.059
"No! They can take nothing from her," the earl said firmly.

11
00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:09.580
Cedric exhaled. "That's a relief.

12
00:01:09.581 --> 00:01:14.223
I wouldn't want her to lose her home or her carriage."

13
00:01:14.224 --> 00:01:19.369
Cedric had to work up his courage to ask another important question.

14
00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:30.032
"That other boy . . . I mean . . . I guess he'll take my place in your life."

15
00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:36.318
"Never!" The earl spoke so fiercely and loudly that Cedric was startled.

16
00:01:36.319 --> 00:01:41.463
"He won't? I mean, I thought—"

17
00:01:41.464 --> 00:01:46.676
Cedric jumped up from his chair and went to his grandfather's side.

18
00:01:46.677 --> 00:01:50.532
"Do you mean I'll still be your boy?"

19
00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:55.949
"My boy!" The earl started to speak, but his voice was shaking.

20
00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:59.858
"Yes, you'll be my boy forever.

21
00:01:59.859 --> 00:02:04.147
Sometimes I feel as if you were the only boy I've ever had."

22
00:02:04.148 --> 00:02:09.100
Cedric broke into a wide grin. "Do you mean that?

23
00:02:09.101 --> 00:02:12.752
Then I don't care whether I'm an earl or not."

24
00:02:12.753 --> 00:02:16.207
The earl laid a hand on Cedric's shoulder.

25
00:02:16.208 --> 00:02:20.249
"I refuse to believe that they can take anything from you.

26
00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:23.241
Or that you can be taken away from me."

27
00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:31.494
Cedric hugged his grandfather tightly. The old man's eyes were wet with tears.

28
00:02:31.495 --> 00:02:38.988
The earl had refused to meet the woman who claimed her son was the real Lord Fauntleroy.

29
00:02:38.989 --> 00:02:42.902
But one day she arrived at the castle with the boy.

30
00:02:42.903 --> 00:02:46.773
At the door she was told by a footman to wait.

31
00:02:46.774 --> 00:02:50.113
A few minutes later, the footman returned.

32
00:02:50.114 --> 00:02:54.880
"The earl refuses to see you. Go away."

33
00:02:54.881 --> 00:03:01.955
The woman looked half-frightened, half-shocked. But she left.

34
00:03:01.956 --> 00:03:08.699
"I didn't even let her in the door," the footman proudly told the other servants.

35
00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:13.768
Later the earl told the story to Mr. Havisham, who had come for lunch.

36
00:03:13.769 --> 00:03:19.990
"The nerve of that woman!" The earl buttered his roll with unusual ferocity.

37
00:03:19.991 --> 00:03:23.402
"Coming here uninvited!"

38
00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:29.223
"I can understand not wanting to receive her here," Mr. Havisham said.

39
00:03:29.224 --> 00:03:32.181
"But I do think you should meet her."

40
00:03:32.182 --> 00:03:35.718
The earl harrumphed.

41
00:03:35.719 --> 00:03:42.398
"She's a bad-tempered, rude woman, but she's not as clever as she thinks.

42
00:03:42.399 --> 00:03:48.704
At times she seems almost overwhelmed by the situation."

43
00:03:48.705 --> 00:03:51.802
Mr. Havisham sipped some water.

44
00:03:51.803 --> 00:03:59.758
"I wonder if she thought she could make this outrageous claim, and we would simply agree to everything."

45
00:03:59.759 --> 00:04:08.033
The earl pointed his fork at the lawyer. "I still don't understand why you want me to meet her."

46
00:04:08.034 --> 00:04:14.148
"We need to investigate this situation further," Mr. Havisham said.

47
00:04:14.149 --> 00:04:21.298
"Let's pay her a visit—and see what she does next."

48
00:04:21.299 --> 00:04:26.592
Mr. Havisham went to the inn where the woman was staying.

49
00:04:26.593 --> 00:04:31.527
He and the earl had agreed to meet in the woman's sitting room.

50
00:04:31.528 --> 00:04:37.379
"The earl will be here in a few minutes," Mr. Havisham said to the woman.

51
00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:42.564
"You should call me Lady Fauntleroy," the woman said.

52
00:04:42.565 --> 00:04:47.781
"I'm pretty sure that's my title now that my son is Lord Fauntleroy, and—"

53
00:04:47.782 --> 00:04:52.773
At that moment the earl stalked into the room.

54
00:04:52.774 --> 00:04:59.695
He towered over the woman as he stared at her. Mr. Havisham introduced them.

55
00:04:59.696 --> 00:05:06.245
"I was just telling your lawyer here that he should call me Lady Fauntleroy," the woman said.

56
00:05:06.246 --> 00:05:09.336
"There are a number of things I want—"

57
00:05:09.337 --> 00:05:14.119
The earl let her talk and make her demands while he said nothing.

58
00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:17.283
When she was finished, he finally spoke.

59
00:05:17.284 --> 00:05:21.615
"You say that you are my older son's wife.

60
00:05:21.616 --> 00:05:29.531
If you can prove that is true, then the law is on your side—your boy is Lord Fauntleroy.

61
00:05:29.532 --> 00:05:34.405
But I guarantee that this matter will be looked into thoroughly.

62
00:05:34.406 --> 00:05:38.436
And, if necessary, we will fight you in court."

63
00:05:38.437 --> 00:05:42.629
The earl continued to glare at the woman.

64
00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:47.859
"If your claims are true, you will be provided for.

65
00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:52.632
But I want to see nothing of you or your son as long as I live.

66
00:05:52.633 --> 00:05:58.575
My castle and tenants will unfortunately have enough of you after my death."

67
00:05:58.576 --> 00:06:02.974
Then he turned his back on her and stalked from the room.

68
00:06:02.975 --> 00:06:08.839
The woman looked pale and shaken.

